# Fix PDF Import & Remove Vercel Limitations

Your PDF import fails because all 40 chunks hit OpenRouter's free-model RATE_LIMIT, and the 240-second Vercel-era global deadline kills the rest. Since you now run on your own Debian server, we can remove all Vercel workarounds and make the import dramatically more reliable.

## Root Cause

From your server logs:
- Chunks 1-7: `RATE_LIMIT` or `invalid JSON` (free models got hammered)
- Chunks 8-40: `Global request timeout reached` (240s Vercel deadline killed them all)

## Proposed Changes

### AI Parser

#### [MODIFY] [aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts)

**Remove Vercel-era restrictions:**
- `GLOBAL_DEADLINE`: Increase from 240s → **600s** (10 minutes). Your server has no timeout limit now!
- `REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS`: Increase from 45s → **90s** per chunk
- `CHUNK_SIZE_CHARS`: Increase from 5000 → **12000** chars. Bigger chunks = fewer API calls = fewer rate limits
- `MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS`: Reduce from 3 → **1**. Sequential processing avoids rate limits entirely on free models
- `REQUEST_INTERVAL_MS`: Increase from 500ms → **2000ms**. Gives OpenRouter breathing room between requests

**Smarter retry with model rotation:**
- When a model returns RATE_LIMIT, automatically switch to the next model in the MODELS list instead of retrying the same rate-limited model

---

### Import Route

#### [MODIFY] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/api/medicines/import/route.ts)

- Remove the 10MB file size limit (your server can handle any size now)

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. After I make the changes, commit and push to GitHub
2. On your Debian terminal, run: `systemctl restart ayurstock`
3. Go to `https://app.vaibhavn8n.dpdns.org/dashboard/medicines`
4. Click Import, upload your PDF, and click "Start Import"
5. Check if the medicines are successfully parsed (it may take 2-5 minutes for large PDFs now, which is fine since there's no timeout!)
